# Target C: direct finite cover excludes the last eight-row Profile B source

Date: 2026-09-22

Classification: **proved candidate awaiting promotion**. This closes the
auxiliary eight-no-root `k=6, D=-1, p=9, d_root=0, d_v=3, q=9` Profile B
source case, conditional only on the already recorded root-block reduction,
the coefficient minimum-weight bound `d_1(P)>=4`, and the source requirement
of nine singleton replacements. It does not close another rank-density
profile, Target C-II, or Level I.

The reduction to `d_1(P)>=4` is recorded on current main in
`target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_weight3_unstripped_closure_2026-09-22.md`.
The Profile B source parameters and virtual complete-block deficiency are in
the active finite-layer records cited there. This note replaces the proposed
five-row weight-three residual audit for this source: that residual is not
needed once the fixed root rows are retained.

## Result

For each rank-two coefficient plane `P <= Q^8` that can occur in this source,
the virtual-canonical complete set has deficiency

```text
d_8 = |C| - rank H(C) != 3
    or fewer than 9 compatible singleton replacements.
```

The full exact cover considered 3,332,125 generator-pair/external-set
instances (duplicates can occur when one source plane has several generating
pairs). It found 47,007 instances with `d_8=3`; every one has singleton
capacity at most eight. The largest capacity at deficiency three was eight.
No candidate satisfies the necessary Profile B source requirements
`d_8=3` and `q=9`.

This is a source-state exclusion. It does not use approximate rank, numerical
optimization, or a packing configuration. It closes this one finite
rank-density case if the inherited reduction is applicable as stated.

## 1. Exact finite universe

There are 35 root blocks, the triples of `K_7`, and three singleton states on
each block. For block `b` and singleton state `s`, write its coefficient
constraint as the row

```text
f_(b,s)[e] = det(local_direction_s, QCOMP[e,b]),
                 e in the 105 no-root four-cycles.
```

Each row has entries in `{0,+1,-1}` and support exactly eight: each of the
four four-sets containing the root triangle supplies three four-cycle
orientations, and precisely one orientation has local quotient direction
parallel to the singleton direction. The other two give nonzero entries.

An empty block contributes the two local coordinate rows. Those rows are in
the span of the three singleton constraints on the same block. Complete and
pair states contribute no coefficient constraints. It follows that every
actual rank-two source plane `P` is spanned by two linearly independent rows
from this fixed list of 105 templates. The empty-state case on one block is
included by choosing two independent templates on that same block.

Thus it is enough to choose an unordered pair of distinct templates and an
eight-element subset `E` of the 105 cycle coordinates, require the restricted
rows to have rank two, and test the resulting row space. The cover may include
planes that are not realizable by a full root state; including them only makes
the exclusion stronger.

## 2. Minimum-weight filter and exact subset count

For a selected set of eight columns from two template rows, each column is
zero or has one of the four projective directions

```text
(1,0), (0,1), (1,1), (1,-1).
```

If `k` selected columns are nonzero and the largest projective class has size
`m`, the minimum weight of a nonzero word in the restricted rank-two row
space is exactly `k-m`: the word annihilating that projective direction
vanishes on precisely its members and on the zero columns. The inherited
bound `d_1(P)>=4` is therefore equivalent to

```text
k >= 6,
every projective class has size <= k-4.
```

For each template pair, the verifier enumerates all choices of `k=6,7,8`
nonzero columns satisfying these multiplicity bounds and all choices of
`8-k` zero columns. Its independent integer combinatorial count is
`3,332,125` over the nine representatives below, matching the C++ visit
count exactly. The multiplicity condition also guarantees restricted rank
two: a rank-one restriction would have all its nonzero columns in one
projective class and minimum word weight zero.

## 3. Nine template-pair orbits

The symmetric group on the seven non-root vertices acts on templates as
marked triangles: a template is a triangle together with the vertex opposite
the root in its defining root four-cycle. Two unordered pairs are in the same
orbit exactly when the triangle intersection size and marked-vertex pattern
agree. The nine types are:

| Triangle intersection | Mark pattern | Pair count |
|---:|---|---:|
| 0 | both marks outside | 630 |
| 1 | neither mark on the common vertex | 1,260 |
| 1 | exactly one mark on it | 1,260 |
| 1 | both marks on it | 315 |
| 2 | both marks outside the intersection | 210 |
| 2 | one mark inside, one outside | 840 |
| 2 | both marks inside, same vertex | 420 |
| 2 | both marks inside, distinct vertices | 420 |
| 3 | same triangle, distinct marks | 105 |
| **Total** |  | **5,460** |

The driver enumerates all `choose(105,2)=5,460` template pairs, constructs one
representative for each type, then independently applies all 5,040 vertex
permutations to each representative. It asserts the nine orbit sizes shown
above and their total. Vertex relabeling changes cycle orientations only by
coordinate signs and changes each local basis by an invertible integral
`A_2` symmetry; it preserves the restricted code weights, local containment,
and complete-block relation rank. Therefore the nine representatives cover
all template-pair/external-set cases.

## 4. Virtual completion and exhaustive output

For each selected external set and its rank-two plane, the verifier computes
the touched root blocks. A touched block is virtual-empty precisely when both
of its empty-state constraint rows lie in `P`; otherwise it is virtual
complete. For each virtual-complete block it tests all three singleton
constraints for membership in `P`. A block admitting one such state
contributes one to singleton capacity; uniqueness follows because two
independent singleton constraints would make the empty block compatible and
therefore virtual-empty.

The C++ implementation uses exact integer plane membership. It computes
`d_8=|C|-rank H(C)` modulo the prime `1,000,000,007`. Every complete-block row
has squared norm at most 12 and each relevant minor has order at most 15.
Hadamard gives absolute determinant at most `12^(15/2)`, less than the prime.
The program checks `prime^2 > 12^15` and verifies primality by trial division;
thus a rational nonzero minor cannot vanish modulo the prime, and the computed
rank equals the rank over `Q`.

The full run reported:

```text
template-pair/external-set instances                     3,332,125
instances with singleton capacity at least 9              2,772,191
instances with virtual deficiency 3                          47,007
deficiency-3 capacity histogram
  0: 2,313; 2: 5,049; 3: 8,055; 4: 5,724; 5: 5,400;
  6: 7,938; 7: 9,450; 8: 3,078
deficiency-3 instances with capacity at least 9                   0
```

For the first two deficiency-three cases in each pair orbit, the Python
driver independently rebuilds the coefficient plane and virtual-complete set
and checks its deficiency and singleton capacity over exact rational
arithmetic. Ten such checks passed. The count of all visited subsets is also
checked independently by the Python binomial sum over four projective
directions.

## 5. Reproduction and scope

Run

```text
python3 research/verify_target_c_profile_b_template_cover_2026_09_22.py --require-no-survivors
```

The driver compiles `target_c_profile_b_template_cover.cpp` with `g++ -O3` in a
temporary directory, enumerates all nine orbits, and fails if any deficiency
three state has capacity at least nine. The C++ rank decisions are exact over
`Q` by the certificate above; the ten independent sample checks use rational
arithmetic. The driver imports the core four-cycle module and requires neither
NumPy nor floating-point arithmetic.

The result excludes only the stated eight-row `k=6` Profile B case in the
support-seven/global-segment-relative auxiliary rank-density route. It does
not close neighboring `k` or support values, the route's global implication,
Target C-II, or Level I.